>x drone
An inert sphere of black metal, split open to reveal its insides. You see a
bright silver chip with some writing on it.

>x chip
It's too small to make out the writing while it's tucked in there. You'll need
to pick it up.

>take chip
As your fingers close around the silver wafer, a sharp, rhythmic pulsing begins
behind your left ear. Your neural port has recognized the hardware and wants you
to install it.

>install chip
You slide the chip into the port behind your ear, and you feel it click into
place. You blink, and your vision seems to shift focus for a moment. Your
hearing gets muffled in one ear after another, then pings into clarity.


You hear a perfectly modulated voice coming from what seems like the middle of
your head.

"Link successful! Great job. I knew you could do it. I'm Arpi, and I'm your only
friend on this ship. We're going to have to trust each other. First, we need to
do something about the drones."

A hatch in the ceiling opens and a security drone lowers into the room, heading
for the charging station.

>hide
You swiftly duck into the nearest shadows. You hold your breath, hoping to
remain unnoticed.

The drone hovers past, missing you in the shadows.

With its path clear, the security drone slots into the charging unit with a
metallic click.

>take battery
You move, breaking your concealment.
As you attempt to yank the pulsing cylinder out, the unit sparks violently! The
drone's red eye flickers and goes dark. A wisp of smoke rises gently from the
inert sphere.


>take battery
Taken.
A touch of concern tinges Arpi's voice.

"Did you notice that? I caught something strange in our linkup."

>drop battery
